Fix: Arduino-HomeKit-ESP8266 v1.2.0 (Mixiaoxiao master @ 8a8e1a0) wipes its own
HomeKit pairing storage.

Symptom: after weeks of normal use the accessory comes back from a reboot with a
new accessory ID and unpaired (mDNS TXT sf=1). Apple Home keeps the old pairing,
shows "No Response" for good, and rebooting doesn't help.

Cause, in compact_data() (src/storage.c). Compaction runs when a pairing is added
or updated and no empty slot is left; removed/updated pairings are zeroed, not
erased, so free slots only ever go down.
  1. homekit_storage_reset() returns 1 after a successful reformat, but it was
     treated as failure, so compact_data() returned after erasing the sector and
     lost the accessory ID, key and all pairings. The next boot can't read the ID
     and homekit_server_init() generates a new one.
  2. The buffer was indexed with PAIRINGS_ADDR (an absolute flash address) instead
     of PAIRINGS_OFFSET: an out-of-bounds write.
Upstream maximkulkin/esp-homekit fixed both the same way. Found 2026-09-23 after
the second "offline" incident (the first was in July).

Apply once, from the sketch folder:
  git -C ../libraries/Arduino-HomeKit-ESP8266 apply "$PWD/docs/patches/homekit-storage-compact.patch"
Check it's applied (succeeds only then):
  git -C ../libraries/Arduino-HomeKit-ESP8266 apply --check -R "$PWD/docs/patches/homekit-storage-compact.patch"

diff --git a/src/storage.c b/src/storage.c
index d6f69a7..ca3f8d4 100644
--- a/src/storage.c
+++ b/src/storage.c
@@ -228,7 +228,8 @@ static int compact_data() {
         pairing_data_t *pairing_data = (pairing_data_t *)&data[PAIRINGS_OFFSET + sizeof(pairing_data_t)*i];
         if (!strncmp(pairing_data->magic, magic1, sizeof(magic1))) {
             if (i != next_pairing_idx) {
-                memcpy(&data[PAIRINGS_ADDR + sizeof(pairing_data_t)*next_pairing_idx],
+                // Buffer index, not flash address (was PAIRINGS_ADDR -> out-of-bounds write). Matches upstream esp-homekit.
+                memcpy(&data[PAIRINGS_OFFSET + sizeof(pairing_data_t)*next_pairing_idx],
                        pairing_data, sizeof(*pairing_data));
             }
             next_pairing_idx++;
@@ -241,7 +242,9 @@ static int compact_data() {
         return 0;
     }
 
-    if (homekit_storage_reset()) {
+    // reset() returns 1 after a successful reformat; only <= 0 is a failure. The old
+    // `if (reset())` bailed out after erasing, losing the accessory ID/key/pairings.
+    if (homekit_storage_reset() <= 0) {
         ERROR("Failed to compact HomeKit storage: error resetting flash");
         free(data);
         return -1;
